Q1. International Tea Day is observed on which date every year?
    May 12
    May 17
    May 21 ✅
    May 31
Ex: International Tea Day = May 21. Theme 2026: 'Sustaining Tea, Supporting Communities'. Organized by FAO. Tea is world's 2nd most consumed beverage after water.

Q2. Who launched the 'Hauslon Ki Udaan 2026-27' Talent Hunt Scheme for Delhi's youth?
    Rekha Gupta ✅
    Atishi
    Manish Sisodia
    Arvind Kejriwal
Ex: Rekha Gupta (Delhi CM) launched Hauslon Ki Udaan 2026-27 — ₹10 Crore Talent Hunt Scheme covering classical music, dance, fine arts, sculpture and theater.

Q3. NISM (National Institute of Securities Markets) was established by which regulatory body?
    RBI
    NABARD
    IRDAI
    SEBI ✅
Ex: NISM established by SEBI. HQ: Navi Mumbai. Provides financial market education and certifications.

Q4. How many climbers scaled Mount Everest from Nepal side in a single day to set a new world record?
    200
    274 ✅
    318
    156
Ex: 274 climbers scaled Everest in a single day — new world record. 3 Indian mountaineers: Tulsi, Sandeep, and Ajay.

Q5. UMMID Program was organized by which department?
    Department of Health Research
    Department of Pharmaceuticals
    Department of Biotechnology ✅
    Department of Science and Technology
Ex: UMMID organized by Dept of Biotechnology under Ministry of Science and Technology. Launched UMMID Sankalan and UMMID Dashboard.

Q6. Bharat Forge's proposed Marine Gas Turbine Repair and Development Complex will be located in which city?
    Visakhapatnam ✅
    Chennai
    Kochi
    Mumbai
Ex: Bharat Forge signed MoU with AP Govt for Marine Gas Turbine Complex at Visakhapatnam — within AP Defence Manufacturing Corridor.

Q7. What is the capital of Cyprus, whose President inaugurated Eurobank's India office in Mumbai?
    Athens
    Valletta
    Limassol
    Nicosia ✅
Ex: Cyprus capital = Nicosia. Currency: Euro. President: Nikos Christodoulides (8th President, since Feb 2023).

Q8.
Statement 1: Coal, Crude Oil, Natural Gas, and Refinery Products all registered negative growth in April 2026.

Statement 2: IIP (Index of Industrial Production) is released by DPIIT on the 12th of every month.

Statement 3: Steel, Cement, and Electricity registered positive growth among the 8 core sectors in April 2026.

👉 Which of the above statements is/are correct?
(a) Only 1 and 2
(b) Only 1 and 3 ✅
(c) 1, 2 and 3
(d) Only 2 and 3
Ex: St1 True - all 4 energy/fuel sectors had negative growth. St2 False - IIP released by NSO (MoSPI), not DPIIT. St3 True - Steel, Cement, Electricity had positive growth.

Q9. Anti-Terrorism Day observed on May 21 marks the death anniversary of which Prime Minister of India?
    Indira Gandhi
    Rajiv Gandhi ✅
    Lal Bahadur Shastri
    VP Singh
Ex: Rajiv Gandhi (7th PM of India) was assassinated on May 21, 1991 in Sriperumbudur, Tamil Nadu by LTTE. India's youngest PM; Bharat Ratna (1991).

Q10. Rekha Gupta is the how many-th Chief Minister of Delhi?
    7th
    8th
    9th ✅
    10th
Ex: Rekha Gupta is Delhi's 9th CM. BJP MLA from Shalimar Bagh. Assumed office February 20, 2025. Delhi LG: Taranjit Singh Sandhu.

Q11. DICGC insures bank deposits up to what amount per depositor?
    ₹5 Lakh ✅
    ₹1 Lakh
    ₹2 Lakh
    ₹10 Lakh
Ex: DICGC insures deposits up to ₹5 Lakh per depositor — protects depositors against bank failure. RBI subsidiary.

Q12. India and Italy will celebrate 'Year of Culture and Tourism' in which year?
    2025
    2026
    2028
    2027 ✅
Ex: India-Italy will celebrate 'Year of Culture and Tourism' in 2027. PM Modi visited Italy as part of his 5-nation tour.

Q13. What is the full form of UMMID, a program dedicated to the nation in New Delhi?
    Unique Method of Monitoring Inherited Diseases
    Unique Method of Management of Inherited Disorders ✅
    Universal Medical Management for Inherited Deficiencies
    Unified Mission for Management of Inherited Disorders
Ex: UMMID = Unique Method of Management of Inherited Disorders. Improves diagnosis and management of rare genetic disorders like Thalassemia and Sickle Cell Anemia.

Q14. Which company manufactured the Vayuastra-1 Loitering Munition System tested in May 2026?
    HAL
    BDL (Bharat Dynamics Limited)
    Nibe ✅
    L&T Defence
Ex: Vayuastra-1 manufactured by Nibe — Pune-based private defence company. Tested at Pokhran (Rajasthan), Joshimath and Malari (Uttarakhand).

Q15. Eurobank opening a representative office in Mumbai is historic for being the first bank from which region to enter India?
    South-East Europe ✅
    Eastern Europe
    Central Europe
    Northern Europe
Ex: Eurobank (Greek bank, HQ Athens) = first bank from South-East Europe in India. Inaugurated by Cyprus President Nikos Christodoulides at Taj Mahal Palace Hotel.

Q16. India has how many Defence Industrial Corridors and in which states?
    2 — Gujarat and Rajasthan
    3 — AP, UP and Tamil Nadu
    2 — Maharashtra and Karnataka
    2 — Andhra Pradesh and Uttar Pradesh ✅
Ex: India has 2 Defence Industrial Corridors — one in Andhra Pradesh and one in Uttar Pradesh. Goal: Make India a global defence manufacturing hub.

Q17. IICA operates under which Ministry?
    Ministry of Finance
    Ministry of Corporate Affairs ✅
    Ministry of Commerce and Industry
    Ministry of Science and Technology
Ex: IICA under Ministry of Corporate Affairs. HQ: Manesar, Haryana. Signed MoU with NISM for corporate governance, ESG and capital markets programs.

Q18. India is the 2nd largest tea producer in the world after which country?
    Sri Lanka
    Kenya
    China ✅
    Vietnam
Ex: India is 2nd largest tea producer after China. Major tea states: Assam, West Bengal (Darjeeling), Tamil Nadu, Kerala.

Q19. BRBNMPL (RBI subsidiary) manages currency note printing presses at which two locations?
    Mysuru and Nasik
    Nasik and Dewas
    Mysuru and Salboni ✅
    Salboni and Dewas
Ex: BRBNMPL manages presses at Mysuru (Karnataka) and Salboni (West Bengal). Nasik and Dewas are managed by SPMCIL (Govt of India).

Q20. Vayuastra-1 is a Loitering Munition System — what is its other commonly used name?
    Ballistic missile
    Cruise missile
    UCAV (Unmanned Combat Aerial Vehicle)
    Kamikaze drone ✅
Ex: Loitering munition = Kamikaze or suicide drone. It loiters over a target area and dives into it to destroy the target.

Q21. Bharat Tex 2026 is organized by a consortium of how many Textile Export Promotion Councils?
    7
    11 ✅
    15
    9
Ex: Bharat Tex Trade Federation = consortium of 11 Textile Export Promotion Councils with Ministry of Textiles support. Scheduled in New Delhi, July 2026.

Q22. Shirui Lily, gifted to Italian PM Giorgia Meloni during PM Modi's visit, is the state flower of which state?
    Nagaland
    Mizoram
    Manipur ✅
    Arunachal Pradesh
Ex: Shirui Lily = state flower of Manipur. Found only on Shirui Kashong peak, Ukhrul district. Critically endangered.

Q23. What is the combined weight of the 8 core sectors in India's overall IIP?
    40.27% ✅
    35.50%
    45.63%
    50.00%
Ex: 8 core sectors have combined weight of 40.27% in IIP. Core sector data released by DPIIT (Ministry of Commerce and Industry).

Q24.
Statement 1: DICGC stands for Deposit Insurance and Credit Guarantee Corporation.

Statement 2: The RBI was established on April 1, 1935 and nationalized on January 1, 1949.

Statement 3: C.D. Deshmukh was the first Indian Governor of RBI and also the 2nd Governor overall.

👉 Which of the above statements is/are correct?
(a) Only 1 and 2 ✅
(b) 1, 2 and 3
(c) Only 2 and 3
(d) Only 1 and 3
Ex: St1 True - correct full form of DICGC. St2 True - RBI est. 1935, nationalized 1949. St3 False - C.D. Deshmukh was 3rd Governor (not 2nd) and 1st Indian Governor.

Q25.
Statement 1: IMEC was launched at the G20 Summit held in Mumbai in 2023.

Statement 2: Italy's PM Giorgia Meloni is the first female Prime Minister of Italy.

Statement 3: Muga Silk, a GI-tagged product presented to Italian PM Meloni by PM Modi, is produced only in Sikkim.

👉 Which of the above statements is/are correct?
(a) Only 1 and 2
(b) 1, 2 and 3
(c) Only 2 ✅
(d) Only 1 and 3
Ex: St1 False - IMEC launched at G20 New Delhi 2023, not Mumbai. St2 True - Giorgia Meloni is Italy's 1st female PM (since Oct 2022). St3 False - Muga Silk is GI-tagged and produced only in Assam.
